# Canonical line endings are LF everywhere (index, checkout, CI).
#
# The repo is edited on Windows and built on Linux; with git's global
# `core.autocrlf=true` the two disagree, and files that are byte-identical
# after normalisation still show up as modified forever. Declaring the rule
# here makes the working tree match the index, so `git status` only reports
# real edits. `git config core.autocrlf false` (repo-local) is the companion
# setting for a Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.p12 binary
*.jks binary
